<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The Planning tab, against MoveIt's own Planning tab group for group:

    Commands            [&Plan] [&Execute] [Plan && Execute] [&Stop]   [OURS]
    Query               "Planning Group:" "Start State:" "Goal State:"  [OURS]
    Path Constraints    a constraint-profile combo                        [NO EQUIVALENT]
    Options             "Planning Time (s):" "Planning Attempts:"
                        "Velocity Scaling:" "Accel. Scaling:" + 6
                        checkboxes                                        [PARTLY OURS]

  The two deliberate deviations, both because curobo's server has no service
  for them:

  * "Path Constraints" is absent. Path constraints are a profile the planner
    interpolates a Cartesian path against; curobo's TrajectoryGoal has no such
    field, so a combo would select nothing.
  * "Options" keeps ONE of MoveIt's five numbers. Planning Time and Planning
    Attempts are search-budget knobs with no curobo equivalent on the classic
    path, and num_seeds / waypoint_tolerance are REJECTED by the server's
    _validate_planning_options, so exposing them would be a control that
    silently fails. Velocity and Acceleration scaling DO exist, and are the one
    row here ("Speed (Time dilatation)"). The rest of the Options group is
    checkboxes, which a single checkbox already stands in for elsewhere on this
    panel (the Context tab's collision-sphere toggle).

  The "Query" group holds the goal POSE rather than MoveIt's three state
  selectors, because MoveIt edits the goal pose on an interactive marker in the
  3D view, not inline: its "Goal State:" combo picks WHICH state, and the pose
  itself belongs to the MotionPlanningRequest dialog. curobo's panel has no
  marker, so the pose has to be typed here, and a QFormLayout row is the
  cheapest honest place for it. The row label is MoveIt's own "Goal State:".

  The bare triples follow MoveIt's Workspace group, which puts three
  unlabelled spinboxes under "Center (XYZ):" and three under "Size (XYZ):" —
  the components are named in the row label, not repeated per field.
-->
